<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marco Sanudo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1227</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marco Sanudo was a Venetian nobleman, nephew of the doge <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enrico-dandolo">Enrico Dandolo</a>, who took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>. Around 1207 he led a private expedition that conquered Naxos and other islands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyclades">Cyclades</a>, founding the Duchy of the Archipelago. He granted islands such as Andros to his companions as fiefs, and his family ruled the duchy until 1383.</p></div>
